 "coverage_notes": {
  "adjudication": "Partly covered. Federal Register notices of hearings, applications, licensing and filings, plus SEC in-house administrative proceedings. Individual ALJ and board decisions (for example, most NLRB decisions) are usually NOT published in the Federal Register and are not tracked in this version.",
  "enforcement": "Partly covered. Only enforcement matters published in the Federal Register (for example, some FTC proposed consent orders and civil-penalty notices) and, for the SEC, its official litigation-release and administrative-proceeding feeds. Most other agencies announce enforcement actions only on their own websites, which this version does not read.",
  "other": "Everything else the Federal Register publishes for the agency (meetings, information-collection requests, and similar notices).",
  "presidential": "Well covered. Executive orders, memoranda and proclamations published in the Federal Register.",
  "rulemaking": "Well covered. Proposed and final rules must be published in the Federal Register, which is checked for every tracked agency. Guidance and policy statements appear only if the agency chose to publish them there."
